Design a clock divider that reduces the input clock frequency to create a 50 MHz output clock signal. The module takes an input clock signal and utilizes a 32-bit register to count the number of rising edges of that input clock. The least significant bit of the counter (clkdiv[0]) is assigned to the output, effectively generating a clock signal that toggles at half the frequency of the input clock, thus achieving the desired clock division.
