description:
Design a digital delay line circuit with N stages. The circuit receives an input signal and a reference clock, shifting the input through a series of N flip-flops on each rising edge of the clock. The output is taken from the first flip-flop in the chain, effectively introducing a delay to the input signal equal to the propagation time of the flip-flops used in the design. This module is useful in applications requiring signal timing adjustments or synchronization.
module top_module(
  input in,
  input ref_clk,
  output reg out
);

